sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch04-18> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Because every area is already fully stocked, as a favoured form increases in number the less favoured forms decrease and become rare, and rarity precedes extinction.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Favoured forms make less favoured forms rare, and rarity precedes extinction";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Charles Darwin, On the Origin of Species (1st ed., London: John Murray, 1859), Chapter IV, “Natural Selection”; section “Extinction caused by Natural Selection”. Scope: species in fully occupied areas, over ecological and geological time"
}
